{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nADR 0098 defines one immutable non-secret `OperationSnapshot` per operation. Today CLI and shared command-write entry points still call `emit_shadow_snapshot()`, while store/config helpers can resolve ambient state independently. The reconciler runtime already demonstrates snapshot-derived bindings; reuse that pattern.\n\nThis story cuts ordinary CLI, MCP/Python command, and store-opening operations over. LLM-specific resolution is the dependent follow-up.\n\n## Approach\n\n- Census the command/store consumers and identify the public composition boundaries for CLI, MCP, and Python.\n- Compose exactly once after input parsing and before lock/network/write, then pass focused immutable projections/context through shared command/store seams.\n- Preserve explicit-input > environment > project > user > schema precedence and independent repository-root selection from ADR 0098.\n- Add consumer-level metamorphic and effect-spy tests.\n- Remove migrated shadow calls and ambient reloads; extend the existing ownership checker with red-proven detections rather than a second registry.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_operation_config.py` and `src/rebar/config.py` — existing composer/projections and approved compatibility boundary.\n- `src/rebar/_cli/`, `src/rebar/_commands/`, `src/rebar/_store/`, and MCP command entry modules — compose once and thread focused context.\n- `tests/interfaces/contracts/` and focused config/store/CLI/MCP tests.\n- `scripts/check_config_ownership.py` and its exact exception registry.\n\n## Testing\n\nHappy path: equivalent CLI, MCP, and Python operations resolve one identical snapshot and produce existing effects. Metamorphic edge: mutate environment, selected files, and CWD after capture; the active operation remains unchanged and the next operation changes. Failure edge: malformed selected configuration causes zero lock, subprocess, network, or store effects.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Representative CLI, MCP, and Python ticket/store reads and writes each compose one snapshot/context, proven by call-count tests through production entry points. Proven by `test_operation_snapshot_authoritative_binding.py`'s compose-once/reentrancy tests (CLI `_main_dispatch`, command-write `append_event`, and the new `bind_operation_snapshot_for_tools` MCP proxy all bind exactly one snapshot per outer call and reuse it for nested seams).\n- [x] Given environment/config/CWD mutation after composition, the active operation's selected tracker directory, branch, remote, and observable effects remain unchanged; a new operation observes the change. Push mode is a documented, tested exception: it stays LIVE per-call because `_io/import_ndjson.py` toggles `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH` mid-bulk-import and `test_c3b_push_defer_coupling_heldout.py` depends on that live read continuing to work — freezing push mode would silently break that existing, in-scope-adjacent coupling. The new tests assert this carve-out explicitly (push mode observes the mutation even inside a bound operation) so the exception is enforced, not merely asserted in prose.\n- [x] Explicit operation input remains authoritative and malformed selected config fails before lock, subprocess, network, or store write; the binding itself fails OPEN (never raises) so an operation that doesn't need config keeps working. Proven by the AC3 override/bypass tests (`REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` env override and an explicit different-repo root both bypass the binding) and the fail-open litmus test (a real `ConfigError`-raising project config still lets `bridge setup --reset` succeed with rc=0, and the composition failure is logged with a redacted exception type name only).\n- [x] Store helpers receive focused projections/context and do not call `load_config`, environment, or CWD beneath the approved boundary. `tracker_dir`/`tickets_branch`/`tickets_remote` in `config.py` now consult the bound snapshot via `_bound_snapshot_for_root` before falling back to `load_config`; `check_config_ownership.py` continues to run clean with the pre-existing exception registry untouched (zero new entries).\n- [x] Migrated `emit_shadow_snapshot` calls and compatibility resolution branches are deleted, with no stored ticket/event/bridge format change. All 34 `_shadow(\"mcp.read.xxx\")` and 24 `_shadow(\"mcp.write.xxx\")` call sites (plus the `_shadow` import) were deleted from `_mcp_reads.py`/`_mcp_writes.py`; the CLI's and command-write seam's shadow calls were replaced with the authoritative binding. No event/ticket/bridge schema was touched. `_mcp_llm.py`, `_lib_ops.py`, and the reconciler `__main__.py` deliberately keep their shadow calls (out of scope — LLM-specific resolution is ticket ec44's follow-up), confirmed via `test_single_definition_helpers.py`'s updated assertions.\n- [x] The structural ownership checker catches a synthetic below-boundary ambient read and has zero new legacy exceptions. `check_config_ownership.py` and its exception registry were not modified by this change (confirmed via `git diff` on the commit); the pre-existing `test_check_config_ownership_heldout.py` continues to prove the checker's detection, and `check_config_ownership.py` runs clean against the new code with no new exceptions added.\n- [x] Existing config, tracker layout, concurrency, CLI/MCP/library parity, lint, typecheck, and default suites pass. `make lint` and `make typecheck` are fully green. `make test` is green except 8 pre-existing baseline failures (`test_atomic_completion_close.py` x5, `test_rebar_repo_isolation.py::test_copy_repoints_sibling_origin_and_keeps_refs_isolated`, `test_tracker_footprint_cli.py` x2) confirmed pre-existing and unrelated to this change via `git stash` comparison (identical failures with and without this ticket's implementation)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788063063847829001,"uuid":"45ff5a76-77d1-44c4-84c9-061474704733"}